Z||000022||kslish||07-08-2001||03:11 AM||||It's an absolute shame that Chrysler abandoned the development of the turbo 2.2-2.5L 4 cyl.  They did away with it just when they were getting it right:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.pinnaclecda.com/Richards_1992_RT_engine.JPG"> <P>This is the 224hp single intercooled turbo, 16-valve Lotus designed head, twin counter-rotating balance shafts version that appeared in the Dodge Spirit R/T and the Daytona R/T.  It's a pretty rare engine (less than 10,000 total made I think).  I looked at a Spirit years ago that had that engine in it....it easily went 0-60 in about 5.5-6.0 seconds.  Even more interesting than the 224hp was the 217lb-ft of torque at a low 2800rpm.<P>Too bad the engine costs $5000 from the dealer....<P>Ken S.<p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 07-08-2001).]||||reg||1
